<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15440" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἅρπυιαι</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρεπ-</span> on a vase from Aegina, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Arch.Zeit.</u>
			40.197
		</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
			<u>EM</u>
			138.21
		</span></i>, and prob. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρέπυιαι
		ἀνηρέψαντο</span> shd. be read in <i><span class="en">
			Od.
		</span></i> ll. cc.; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνερείπομαι</span>
			) αἱ, <i>the Snatchers,</i> a name
			used in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> to personify <i>whirlwinds</i> or <i>hurricanes</i> (so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφῶσι καὶ ἁρπυίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.333
				</span></i>
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅρπυιαι ἀνηρείψαντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.241
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				20.77
			</span></i>: acc. pl., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				267
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτηνά τ᾽ Ἁρπυιῶν γένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anaxil.
					22.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.188
			</span></i>: rarely in sg., <i><span class="en">
				Euph.
				113
			</span></i>: as pr. n., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἅρπυια
			Ποδάργη,</span> mother of the horses of Achilles, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.150
			</span></i>; also name of one of Actaeon's hounds, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				245
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁρπυίας: ἁρπακτικοὺς κύνας,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁ. σκύλακες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Inscr.Perg.</u>
					203
				</span></i>
			. (A quasi-participial form.)</div>
